  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1051 AM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nOne more (short-lived) shot of heat and humidty is expected to rear \nits head again on Wednesday as the boundary layer swings back around \nto the southwest. Afternoon highs will creep a few degrees warmer \nthan normal, but that should be about it. Cooler weather will \nfollow! BUT -- the door may be open for showers and storms, too. \nMost are suggesting a Wednesday night into Thursday time frame now \nfor more widespread storm development. Forecast soundings on \nThursday are worth watching as mid-level lapse rates are healthy and \nthere could be *a little* more shear to work with.\n\nThis storm potential on Wednesday night and Thursday all revolves \naround the development of a large upper level trough over the \neastern half of the US and once we get past these mid-week storms, \nmost medium range guidance suggests temperatures right around normal \nwith small to no rain chances for the upcoming weekend. Something to \nlook forward to if you have outdoor plans!",
